I open the door to my home.
Asha is outside with the dog Moti.
Moti wags his tail enthusiastically.
"Asha, please come inside," I say.
Asha and Moti come inside.
I serve the new fusion food.
Asha tastes the food.
"Maya, this food is very delicious!" she says.
"It has Mexican food and Indian spices in it," I say.
During the meal, we discuss our plans for the weekend.
Asha wants to go to the market tomorrow.
"We can go for an outing tomorrow," she says.
"Okay, this is a good plan," I say.
Then Moti comes under the table.
He looks at me with big eyes.
He wants some food from my plate.
I say, "Moti, this is not for you!"
Asha laughs loudly.
In January, Mumbai was very new to me.
But now, a quiet night like this is just my normal life.
